Description: Avoid portal self-activation and defer backend activation
The confined frontend's connected desktop slot makes GIO treat it as a
portal client. Suppress that detection while the frontend initializes its
own GIO monitors, so they do not block on the frontend's D-Bus activation.
Restore the snap environment before serving requests. The GTK backend also
needs the GNOME display, but the frontend can start before GNOME Shell
creates it. Avoid starting it while constructing implementation proxies;
proxy method calls can still auto-activate it once the display is ready.
Use the requesting app's permissions ID when registering selected files
with the document portal. Permit AddNamedFull only for the confined session
frontend, whose Documents D-Bus plug is assigned only to that frontend.
Open selected files with the access mode requested by FileChooser so
writable document grants are backed by a writable descriptor.

